---
import Profile from "../layouts/Profile.astro";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
---

<Profile
  slug="inventor"
  related={["quantum-physicist", "wellness-rd", "apps"]}
  intro="I build instruments as well as working with them. The one I can show you best is a telescope I put together to photograph the night sky from a city rooftop."
>
  <section class="folio-row" id="purakaash">
    <div>
      <span class="folio-meta">Field instrument / 2025</span>
      <h2>Purākaash Mk II</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <figure class="field-photo">
        <Photo name="rooftop-telescope" />
        <figcaption>Setting up Purākaash on the rooftop.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        The telescope collects the light. The mount has to keep it pointed at
        the same patch of sky while the camera records a long exposure. My part
        was bringing a 203 mm telescope, tracking mount, cooled camera and
        guiding system together as one instrument.
      </p>
      <p>
        I commissioned it in October 2025 through Master Within. Vishwa Vigyan
        documents the build.
      </p>
      <a href="https://vishwavigyan.com/purakaash.html">
        See the telescope and build record ↗
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="folio-row">
    <h2>Robotics, Vortex &amp; equipment</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Robotics and Vortex are also part of my engineering work. I’m exploring
        new equipment through Vishwa Vigyan and working with wellness companies
        on how to turn an equipment idea into something they can manufacture.
      </p>
      <a href="/wellness-rd/">My role in wellness equipment development →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="folio-row">
    <h2>Back at the lab</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        My research asks how quantum circuits behave when I cool and measure
        them. My physics profile collects the experiments, theory and papers
        behind that side of my work.
      </p>
      <a href="/quantum-physicist/">Explore my physics research →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Profile>
